WEBVTT

00:00.100 --> 00:08.161
Follow a sample higher education deployment from gathering the university's public pages to checking the finished site.

00:08.961 --> 00:17.633
Configure the kit, install it with PowerShell, review SharePoint and Teams, publish a content update, and test the result again.

00:18.433 --> 00:23.513
This is an unofficial demonstration using a synthetic organization profile.

00:23.513 --> 00:30.288
It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or deployed for the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign.

00:30.288 --> 00:35.368
Public university information is used only to show how configuration works.

00:36.168 --> 00:40.098
Everything runs in the Microsoft demonstration lab tenant.

00:40.098 --> 00:48.159
For a real deployment, use your organization's authorized tenant, accounts, app registration, and SharePoint addresses.

00:49.000 --> 00:53.406
Before opening PowerShell, find the official pages users will need.

00:54.206 --> 01:01.636
Collect University of Illinois pages for responsible AI use and data handling, along with Copilot Chat guidance.

01:02.436 --> 01:10.853
Also find the published support contacts, service requests, security and privacy reporting instructions, and training resources.

01:11.653 --> 01:15.401
Record the exact links and the published support mailbox.

01:15.401 --> 01:20.333
For your own deployment, have the organization confirm which routes to use.

01:21.133 --> 01:24.947
Don't invent an internal address or guess the tenant name.

01:24.947 --> 01:30.996
And don't assume the organization's public email domain is also its Microsoft tenant domain.

01:31.767 --> 01:35.620
Keep public information separate from deployment settings.

01:36.420 --> 01:43.994
Public information includes the organization's name, published guidance, support contacts, and training resources.

01:44.794 --> 01:56.951
Deployment settings include the Microsoft tenant, SharePoint hosts, and administrator sign-in, plus the app registration's client ID and any service accounts or production mailboxes.

01:56.951 --> 02:01.203
Have an authorized administrator supply or confirm those values.

02:02.003 --> 02:07.783
The tenant-specific values in this recording belong to the Microsoft demonstration lab.

02:07.783 --> 02:12.168
For a real deployment, use the organization's authorized settings.

02:12.967 --> 02:16.326
Open PowerShell 7 with the No Profile switch.

02:17.126 --> 02:19.662
Select the approved release zip file.

02:19.662 --> 02:25.832
The release receipt supplied with the package records its expected SHA256 hash.

02:25.832 --> 02:30.220
Calculate the file's hash and continue only if the values match.

02:31.020 --> 02:37.053
For each clean run, extract the release into a new, empty install folder on the C drive.

02:37.853 --> 02:42.720
Copy the higher education template into a separate organization folder.

02:42.720 --> 02:51.975
That folder holds settings, content overrides, and approved assets outside the install folder, so a newer release won't overwrite them.

02:52.833 --> 02:57.268
Open Deployment Settings dot JSON in the organization folder.

02:58.068 --> 03:05.481
Enter the tenant, SharePoint admin host, SharePoint site host, owner account, organization name, and alias.

03:06.281 --> 03:11.893
If this is the tenant's first installation, leave PnP client ID blank for now.

03:11.893 --> 03:16.396
Step six registers the provisioning app and saves its client ID.

03:16.396 --> 03:19.930
This recording reuses an existing approved lab app.

03:20.730 --> 03:22.601
Choose the alias carefully.

03:22.601 --> 03:30.638
It becomes the Team alias and SharePoint site path, and it must meet Microsoft 365 naming requirements.

03:31.438 --> 03:34.555
Set Learning Environment to Higher Education.

03:34.555 --> 03:45.364
Keep Team Visibility set to Private and Center of Excellence Site Sharing Capability set to Disabled unless the organization has approved a different setup.

03:46.300 --> 03:50.342
In the same settings file, configure the links users will see.

03:51.142 --> 03:56.813
Use Service Desk for general help and Technology Request for approved service requests.

03:57.613 --> 04:08.174
Point Data Safety Incident to the organization's approved security or privacy reporting instructions, and AI Guidelines to its approved responsible-use guidance.

04:08.974 --> 04:12.038
Add the reviewed governance and training links.

04:12.038 --> 04:19.339
Decide whether to enable the prompt library and developer track, and include only approved champion departments.

04:20.139 --> 04:23.529
Review any sample agent entries before installation.

04:23.529 --> 04:26.593
This lab includes two clearly labeled examples.

04:27.367 --> 04:35.398
Check that you're running PowerShell 7.4 or later, and install PnP PowerShell version 3.2.0.

04:36.198 --> 04:44.355
If the tenant needs a provisioning app, have someone authorized to grant the required app permissions run the registration script.

04:44.355 --> 04:48.998
Then confirm in Entra that all required delegated permissions are granted.

04:48.998 --> 04:52.574
The script saves the new client ID to the settings file.

04:53.374 --> 04:59.021
This lab already has an approved provisioning app, so the recording reuses its client ID.

04:59.821 --> 05:03.335
Before continuing, review any Entra group naming policy.

05:03.335 --> 05:10.425
Confirm who will run the installation, who will own the site, and whether the incident-reporting link is correct.

05:11.267 --> 05:14.440
Run the installer from the extracted kit folder.

05:15.240 --> 05:18.480
Keep the Seed Demo Content switch in the command.

05:18.480 --> 05:22.909
It publishes the pages, catalogs, calendar, and governance content.

05:22.909 --> 05:28.000
Without it, the installer creates only the Team and an empty SharePoint site.

05:28.800 --> 05:33.956
Use Demo mode in this lab to retain the kit's generated demonstration notices.

05:33.956 --> 05:37.659
Use Customer mode for an approved production deployment.

05:37.659 --> 05:43.212
Review the source files and existing site content, and remove sample items yourself.

05:43.212 --> 05:46.319
Changing the mode does not replace that review.

05:47.119 --> 05:51.218
Because this is a new installation, don't use Resume Existing.

05:52.018 --> 05:56.448
If an earlier attempt created a Team or site, stop and investigate.

05:56.448 --> 06:04.645
Either resume that exact deployment, or run zero-four Remove Copilot Center of Excellence dot P S one before starting again.

06:04.645 --> 06:14.099
Deleting only the SharePoint site leaves the Team and Microsoft 365 group behind, so the next installation can conflict with them.

06:15.200 --> 06:20.492
The installer first checks the organization's content files for configuration errors.

06:21.292 --> 06:28.514
It then checks the tenant, owner, group naming policy, and whether the alias is available before creating resources.

06:28.514 --> 06:32.125
In this run, the account could not read the naming policy.

06:32.125 --> 06:35.549
An authorized administrator must confirm it separately.

06:35.549 --> 06:43.767
A naming policy can add a prefix or suffix to the group and alias, which can prevent the installer from finding the Team it created.

06:44.567 --> 06:47.307
Read each stop-or-proceed message carefully.

06:47.307 --> 06:52.474
A decision to proceed here is a recorded lab decision, not approval for production.

06:53.274 --> 07:01.181
After the checks, the installer creates the private Team, its standard and shared channels, and the connected SharePoint sites.

07:01.981 --> 07:06.215
The public video uses reference views for longer provisioning steps.

07:06.215 --> 07:09.016
Keep the full transcript for troubleshooting.

07:09.967 --> 07:13.261
Watch as the installer publishes the site content.

07:14.061 --> 07:26.117
It adds navigation, learning guides, and the support and governance pages, followed by the prompt library, agent showcase, success stories, champions directory, and training calendar.

07:26.917 --> 07:35.152
It also configures catalog approvals, uploads governance drafts, adds resource tabs, and posts the prepared welcome messages.

07:35.952 --> 07:39.708
Finally, it reports the resulting security configuration.

07:40.508 --> 07:50.126
In this recording, the higher education prompt library contains about 230 prompts and takes the longest of the catalog steps shown.

07:50.767 --> 07:55.607
A Team appearing in the tenant doesn't mean the installation is complete.

07:56.407 --> 08:05.490
At the end of a successful run, the installer prints the SharePoint site address and saves deployment records in the organization folder.

08:06.290 --> 08:09.008
Save the site address exactly as printed.

08:09.008 --> 08:12.588
The recorded run finished in about thirty-six minutes.

08:13.388 --> 08:23.532
Check that no error stopped the installation, and confirm that Center of Excellence Revision Report dot JSON names the intended alias and tenant host.

08:24.332 --> 08:30.829
The installer saves that report beside Deployment Settings dot JSON in the organization folder.

08:30.829 --> 08:34.874
It saves the run transcripts in the Revision Audit subfolder.

08:35.667 --> 08:37.444
The installer has finished.

08:37.444 --> 08:38.891
Check what it created.

08:39.691 --> 08:47.983
Run the read-only checker using the same organization folder and content mode, plus the site address printed by the installer.

08:48.783 --> 08:51.876
The checker reads the site without changing it.

08:51.876 --> 09:00.498
It checks the pages, navigation, catalogs, approval and permission settings, configured links, learning content, and site security.

09:00.498 --> 09:04.380
In Demo mode, it also checks for the demonstration notices.

09:05.180 --> 09:07.944
Look for the final All Checks Passed line.

09:08.744 --> 09:13.022
Review every warning and complete the manual check it identifies.

09:13.022 --> 09:16.115
Passing the checker is only part of the review.

09:17.033 --> 09:20.571
Open the site at the address printed by the installer.

09:21.371 --> 09:25.302
On Home, check the main task tiles and demonstration notice.

09:26.102 --> 09:28.264
Open Service Catalog and Support.

09:28.264 --> 09:37.567
Follow the links for general support, technology requests, and data-safety incidents, and confirm that each leads to the approved destination.

09:38.367 --> 09:42.560
On Governance, check the university's public AI guidance links.

09:42.560 --> 09:46.360
Then open the prompt library and review the catalog views.

09:47.160 --> 09:50.501
This recording shows the administrator review only.

09:50.501 --> 09:57.838
Before opening the production site to users, repeat it with an account that has reader access, not owner access.

09:57.838 --> 10:02.883
Also replace every lab-specific value with one the organization has approved.

10:03.800 --> 10:04.518
Open Teams.

10:05.318 --> 10:14.910
The provisioning app can publish welcome messages, but reading them back requires an additional message-reading permission, so check them visually.

10:15.710 --> 10:19.168
Open General, Ask Us Anything, and Share Your Prompt.

10:19.168 --> 10:26.868
Confirm that each channel has exactly one prepared welcome post, follow its links, and check the demonstration notice.

10:27.668 --> 10:35.628
If an interrupted run left a post missing, identify the exact channel before republishing it through the recovery process.

10:36.428 --> 10:40.147
Don't republish all the welcome messages just to be safe.

10:40.147 --> 10:41.909
That can create duplicates.

10:42.700 --> 10:47.921
Use the update script to publish reviewed changes without rebuilding the Team.

10:48.721 --> 10:57.558
This recording also uses Scope All with Repair Captured Pages because it demonstrates the repair process on a fresh validation site.

10:58.358 --> 11:02.173
Repair Captured Pages rewrites the pages the kit manages.

11:02.173 --> 11:06.257
Edits made directly to those pages in SharePoint may be lost.

11:06.257 --> 11:14.959
Before using it on an existing site, review section D, Home and the four captured pages, in zero-one Admin Quickstart dot H T M L.

11:14.959 --> 11:17.770
That section lists what the switch resets.

11:17.770 --> 11:20.515
The update script has no What If preview.

11:21.315 --> 11:23.859
Replace Files needs a separate review.

11:23.859 --> 11:30.820
It can replace every affected governance draft in the run, not just the document you intended to change.

11:31.620 --> 11:40.189
If the saved deployment identity doesn't match the configured tenant and alias, stop and resolve the mismatch before continuing.

11:41.167 --> 11:49.409
After the update, run the checker again and repeat the administrator's SharePoint review and the Teams welcome-post review.

11:50.209 --> 11:57.380
Confirm that the intended changes appeared and that the links, catalog views, and welcome posts still work.

11:58.180 --> 12:11.515
Keep Deployment Settings dot JSON, Center of Excellence Revision Report dot JSON, the Revision Audit run transcripts, automated test results, and manual review records together for the handoff.

12:12.167 --> 12:17.081
The sample installation and update finished, and the automated checks passed.

12:17.881 --> 12:23.433
The administrator's SharePoint review and the Teams welcome-post review were completed.

12:23.433 --> 12:28.921
The group naming policy and reader-account review still require separate confirmation.

12:29.721 --> 12:33.039
Keep the handoff records from step fifteen together.

12:33.039 --> 12:38.719
For recovery or removal, use the administrator quickstart included with the same release.

12:39.519 --> 12:45.709
This was an unofficial demonstration in a Microsoft lab, not a University of Illinois deployment.
